<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>

    <!-- =====================================================================
         The service group carried by the WordPress relay's service user
         (`svc_web_leads`). Together with `base.group_user` — granted on the
         USER, not implied here — it is everything that account needs.

         W1 shipped this group implying `sales_team.group_sale_salesman_all_
         leads`, for two reasons that both turned out to be satisfiable
         without it (W1 review M3):

           (a) `crm.lead` ACLs — now granted directly, below, read/write/
               create and NO unlink;
           (b) escaping the stock *personal-leads* record rule so the dedup
               search can see every open lead. A record rule only restricts
               members of the rule's OWN groups: `crm.crm_rule_personal_lead`
               and `crm.crm_rule_all_lead` are both scoped to the salesman
               groups, so a user in NEITHER is untouched by both and sees
               every lead the multi-company rule allows. Dropping the group
               is therefore not a regression for dedup — it is the same
               visibility by a narrower route.

         What the implication silently also granted, and what dropping it
         takes back: `res.partner` create/write (crm/security/ir.model.
         access.csv), `account.move` + `account.move.line` read (sale/
         security/ir.model.access.csv). Neither has anything to do with
         capturing a contact form.

         Odoo 19 has NO `category_id` on res.groups — groups reference a
         `privilege_id` (conventions §4).
         ===================================================================== -->

    <record id="group_web_leads_service" model="res.groups">
        <field name="name">Web Leads Service</field>
        <field name="privilege_id" ref="health_base.res_groups_privilege_healthcare"/>
        <!-- Ledger §5.69(b): deleting a field from a data record does NOT
             unset it — an update writes only the fields it names. The W1
             implication has to be cleared explicitly, or it survives the
             upgrade. -->
        <field name="implied_ids" eval="[(5, 0, 0)]"/>
        <field name="comment">Machine account group for the website lead-capture endpoint: create and update leads, create touchpoints, read the catchment list, the CRM teams and stages, and the UTM vocabularies. No partner writes, no accounting, no clinical models.</field>
    </record>

</odoo>
